rules_version = '2';

// EOS Cloud Storage -- DENY EVERY CLIENT, EVERYWHERE.
//
// The only objects EOS stores today are inbound email attachments (functions/src/inboundWork/
// attachmentCustody.ts), and no browser reads them from here. The one route to those bytes is the
// governed `getInboundWorkAttachment` callable, which authorizes against the INBOUND REQUEST the
// attachment belongs to and reads the object with the Admin SDK. A person who cannot open the request
// cannot reach its attachment, because there is no client-reachable path to reach it by.
//
// THIS FILE IS THE WHOLE POLICY, and it is deliberately the strictest one that can be written. Admin SDK
// access from a trusted Function bypasses these rules by design, which is exactly the intended shape: the
// server is the only reader, and the server checks authority before it reads.
//
// IF A LATER FEATURE NEEDS CLIENT-VISIBLE FILES, it does not get them by widening this file. It gets a
// governed read of its own, or -- if direct client access is genuinely required -- its own match block,
// its own authorization predicate, and its own Owner-approved review. A blanket read grant here would
// hand every authenticated user every customer's attachments at once.
service firebase.storage {
  match /b/{bucket}/o {
    match /{allPaths=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
